  pageKey="guideCost"
  title="How much does a website cost in Canada? | WEBAO"
  description="How website pricing works in Canada, and what Webao charges: Launch C$89.99/mo, Grow C$149.99/mo, Scale C$349.99/mo, annual billing 2 months free."
  eyebrow="Guides"
  heading="How much does a website cost in Canada?"
  intro="A plain explanation of how website pricing works, and what Webao charges. No market averages, no competitor prices, and no invented ranges. The only concrete prices on this page are Webao's own prices, because those are the only ones verified here."
  answerLine="Launch C$89.99/mo, Grow C$149.99/mo, Scale C$349.99/mo. Annual billing is 2 months free."
  sections={[
    {
      heading: "Who this is for",
      body: "A small business owner in Canada who needs a website and wants to know what the money covers before starting.",
    },
    {
      heading: "Two ways websites are usually priced",
      body: "There are two common pricing models. They are not the same purchase, so comparing only the headline number does not compare the full cost.",
      subsections: [
        {
          heading: "One time build",
          body: "You pay once for the build. After launch, the running costs are usually separate: domain renewal, hosting, security updates, and any later changes. Those later costs depend on who looks after the site and what changes you ask for, so a one time quote on its own does not tell you the yearly cost of keeping the site live.",
        },
        {
          heading: "Monthly plan",
          body: "You pay a monthly fee that covers the build and the ongoing running of the site in one payment. The question to ask with any monthly plan is the same as with a one time build: what exactly is included, for how long is the price fixed, and what happens when the term ends.",
